    "done_when": "Unblock the analytic-certificate booking tests and tighten the sequential-scan guard. The booking-cost review (score 112) left two findings.\n\n- `scripts/prototypes/support/book.py:55`. The shared fixture's cache-key assertion refuses the stored support fixtures, because they carry a superseded identity schema. The six analytic-certificate parametrizations of `tests/test_current_book_vectorised.py` therefore fail before booking, at base and at head, so the closed-form booking identity of §3 is unverified on the certificate carriers.\n- `tests/test_current_book_vectorised.py:411`. The guard against a sequential cell axis asserts only that no lowered scan length equals the fixture's cell count (17). A scan over the cells with any other bound would pass.\n\nDone when all of the following hold:\n(1) The certificate fixtures are rebuilt in-run, or keyed on the current device-built identity, so all six parametrizations reach booking and pass. Never write into the read-only certified caches under the proto-support run directory; build any new fixture under the test's own temporary directory.\n(2) The guard asserts that no scan in the lowered booking program iterates over the cell dimension, whatever its length. Check the scanned operand's leading axis against the cell axis, not a length equality. A negative control lowers a deliberately sequential scan of a different length over the cells, and the guard fails it.\n(3) `tests/test_current_book_vectorised.py` passes by delta against the base. Run it CPU-only, in a fresh process, on the fleet allocation in place, with JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu and configure_dtypes() before any array. Report baseline_suite and after_suite: the six parametrizations fail at base and pass at head, with no other change.\n\nWrite only `scripts/prototypes/support` and `tests/test_current_book_vectorised.py`. Commit with a conventional subject and a body, and write the manifest listing every commit.\n\nRun conditions: H200 rows run as one job through RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 scripts/h200_test_lane/run.sh --log (an absolute path in the run directory) --wait -- (targets), or one sbatch job on --partition=betelgeuse --reservation=gpu_0003_grpA --gres=gpu:1 with rungs as rows inside the allocation (never an array), --time sized to finish, XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false and TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment and in every child; submit for real and read squeue a minute later rather than trusting sbatch --test-only. On a compute node run /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python directly with PYTHONPATH set to the run worktree and never invoke uv; every login-node uv command carries --no-sync and nothing runs uv sync. configure_dtypes() before any array and jax_enable_x64 asserted True. Gates pass by delta against orientation_base_sha in per-module fresh processes, both arms running the same test files with the repository root conftest, baseline_suite and after_suite as single-line JSON whose log_path names one log file and whose command is literally runnable. Any wait is declared on the job that finishes last as wait_probe [\"sacct\",\"-n\",\"-X\",\"-P\",\"-j\",\"(job id)\",\"-o\",\"State\"] and wait_terminal [\"COMPLETED\",\"FAILED\",\"CANCELLED\",\"TIMEOUT\",\"OUT_OF_MEMORY\",\"NODE_FAIL\"] as JSON lists, and names every job it depends on in wait_condition. The certified 550, 2,000 and 5,000-cell machines and exteriors are cached under /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261009T181553786165-proto-support/ordered/rows/cache and may be read in place, never written. Run filepath relativize over any evidence fragment before committing. Commit with conventional subjects and bodies at every step and write the manifest and commit before every job wait; the manifest commits line lists every commit; status is complete, blocked or failed, which the worker sets itself. No plan labels in source names or comments. Inside every job payload, make one directory with mktemp -d /tmp/$USER-$SLURM_JOB_ID-XXXX, point TMPDIR at it, and remove it on exit with trap 'rm -rf' (keep TMPDIR=/tmp in the submit environment so slurmstepd can start). Never leave extracted base trees or caches in /tmp after a node ends; anything a later reader needs goes under the run directory on GPFS.\n\nImport provenance: print nova.__file__ in every log header. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), run CPU work in place. The time budget is per working turn, not a deadline: park on H200 jobs with declared waits and continue across turns; this node is sized at about 8 worker-hours, and an unmeasured item in your own scope is remaining work, not a blocker. Never edit a script a submitted job will run; submit a per-job copy. Size every job memory from a measured row. The manifest commits line lists every commit (git rev-list), orientation_base_sha is copied from git rev-parse output, and status is complete when the record is delivered even if the target is not met (then give the nearest measured figure and what dominates it).",
